      "writtenOn": "2018-02-01T21:22:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have been using typedefs:\n1) to make it easier to change how something is represented without a large refactor. This is balanced by the use static_asserts to explicitly check assumptions whenever possible to make it harder to introduce bugs through type changes later.\n2) to make it easier to catch code errors where data flow isn\u0027t correct since they become type errors.\n3) to keep from having to prefix types with struct.",
